Done. Summary:

**Cause:** In `llm/llama_server.go`, both SSE stream parsers (the completion path at ~line 1506 and the chat path at ~line 1793) read lines directly from `res.Body` and attempted `json.Unmarshal` on any non-empty line that didn't start with `data: `. llama-server sends SSE comment lines (e.g. `: keep-alive` ping comments) to keep idle streams alive; per the SSE spec these are comments to be ignored, but the code tried to parse them as JSON and returned an error, aborting the stream.

**Fix:** In both parser loops, skip lines that begin with `:` (SSE comments):

```go
// Ignore SSE comment lines, e.g. keep-alive ping comments from llama-server.
if bytes.HasPrefix(line, []byte(":")) {
    continue
}
```

**Verification:**
- `go test ./llm/...` → `ok github.com/ollama/ollama/llm`
- Also confirmed `go test ./middleware/... ./openai/... ./anthropic/...` all pass.
